From: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
Subject: [PATCH 0155] ath79: keep legacy ag71xx zero-budget polling TX-only

The selected AG71XX_LEGACY driver reaches receive refill and completion
handling during netpoll zero-budget calls. Keep completed transmit cleanup,
then return before the receive path. Positive-budget polling is unchanged.
Validated by an isolated object compile with the frozen MIPS kernel flags;
netconsole transmission and panic delivery still require hardware testing.

diff --git a/target/linux/ath79/patches-6.12/711-net-ag71xx-legacy-netpoll-zero-budget.patch b/target/linux/ath79/patches-6.12/711-net-ag71xx-legacy-netpoll-zero-budget.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/ath79/patches-6.12/711-net-ag71xx-legacy-netpoll-zero-budget.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx/ag71xx_main.c
++++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx/ag71xx_main.c
+@@ -1378,6 +1378,10 @@
+ 
+ 	tx_done = ag71xx_tx_packets(ag, false, limit);
+ 
++	/* Netpoll invokes NAPI with zero budget for TX cleanup only. */
++	if (!limit)
++		return 0;
++
+ 	DBG("%s: processing RX ring\n", dev->name);
+ 	rx_done = ag71xx_rx_packets(ag, limit);
+ 
